hable AutoByteus node for window access, capability display, and optional remote browser sharing.","settings.components.settings.NodeManager.addedSuccess":"Node added successfully.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.title":"Phone Access","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.description":"Pair a phone/PWA to this desktop over any private network you already trust.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.enable":"Enable Phone Access","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.loading":"Loading Phone Access…","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.disabledNotice":"Phones cannot connect while Phone Access is disabled. Paired-device records are kept, but mobile credentials are rejected until you enable this again.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.reachableServerUrl":"Discovered URL candidates (diagnostic)","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.refreshCandidates":"Refresh candidates","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.manualPrivateNetworkUrl":"Tailscale Serve HTTPS URL","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.useManualUrl":"Use URL","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.baseMobileContract":"Paste the /mobile URL here. AutoByteus stores the clean server base internally and creates the QR with /mobile.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.serveHttpsUrlHelp":"After running Serve/status in the guide, copy the HTTPS MagicDNS hostname, append /mobile, and paste it here. It normally looks like https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net/mobile without :29695.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.candidatePlaceholder":"Paste Serve HTTPS URL above, or choose an HTTPS candidate","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.httpCandidateDiagnosticNote":"HTTP interface candidates such as http://100.x.y.z:29695 or LAN addresses are diagnostics only. The :29695 port belongs to local HTTP reachability, not the Tailscale Serve HTTPS QR target.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.remoteCandidateDiagnosticNote":"Docker/container candidates are diagnostic only in remote-node windows. QR creation requires a manual Android-facing private HTTPS URL mapped to this Docker node.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.remoteAdvertisedUrlVerificationHelp":"Create QR will verify that this HTTPS URL reaches the same Docker node as the desktop management URL before creating a pairing code.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.localManagementTitle":"Automatic local management credential","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.localManagementHelp":"Launcher-managed Docker nodes are authorized automatically from local launcher state. The credential is not shown, copied into QR payloads, or stored in browser storage.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.localManagementRequiredNotice":"This Docker node is not recognized as launcher-managed from local launcher state. Re-add the Backend URL printed by autobyteus-docker, or recreate the node with the current launcher before managing Phone Access.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.httpsRequiredTitle":"HTTPS URL required","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.httpsRequiredBody":"Create QR requires a private HTTPS URL. Paste a Tailscale Serve URL such as https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net/mobile.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.createQrCode":"Create QR code","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokeAllPhones":"Revoke all phones","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokePhone":"Revoke","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairedPhones":"Paired phones","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.deviceViewsAria":"Paired phone views","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.activeDevicesTab":"Active ({{count}})","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokedDevicesTab":"Revoked / History ({{count}})","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairedAt":"Paired {{date}}","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.lastSeenAt":"Last seen {{date}}","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.neverSeen":"never","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokedAt":"Revoked {{date}}","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.noActivePhonesPaired":"No active phones paired yet.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.noRevokedPhones":"No revoked phone history yet.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairingQr":"Pairing QR","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairingQrDescription":"Scan or open this from the phone. It contains a short-lived one-time code, not the long-lived device credential.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.pairingQrAlt":"Phone Access pairing QR","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.noActiveQrCode":"No active QR code.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokeAllConfirm":"Revoke every paired phone? Every phone must pair again.","settings.components.settings.PhoneAccessCard.revokedCredentials":"Revoked {{count}} phone credential(s).","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.eyebrow":"Phone setup","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.title":"Set up private HTTPS phone access","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.description":"Use Tailscale.app on this Mac to Serve AutoByteus at a stable private HTTPS MagicDNS URL before creating a Phone Access QR code.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.targetUrlTitle":"Target mobile URL","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.targetUrlDescription":"After Serve is running, open or paste the mobile shell URL. AutoByteus will normalize it to the server base internally.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.magicDnsGuidance":"Use the full MagicDNS hostname/FQDN shown by Tailscale, such as machine.tailnet.ts.net, for the HTTPS Serve URL. IPv4 and IPv6 are useful diagnostics, but they are not the preferred HTTPS certificate hostname.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.installStepTitle":"1. Install and sign in to Tailscale.app on this Mac","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.macosCliNote":"Use Tailscale.app to sign in and confirm the full MagicDNS hostname/FQDN. AutoByteus only shows copyable commands; it does not run Tailscale or inspect local Tailscale status.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.macosCommandsTitle":"2. Run Tailscale Serve on this Mac","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.macosCommandsDescription":"Run the background Serve command, then run Serve status and copy the HTTPS MagicDNS URL. Append /mobile before pasting it into Phone Access below.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.platform.macos":"macOS","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.platformDescription.macos":"Install Tailscale.app, sign in, and use the direct app commands below for Serve.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeForeground.title":"macOS app: Serve in foreground","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeForeground.description":"Starts Serve through the Tailscale.app executable while the command remains running.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeBackground.title":"macOS app: Serve in background","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeBackground.description":"Starts Serve through the Tailscale.app executable and keeps it running after Terminal closes.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeStatus.title":"macOS app: Inspect Serve status","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeStatus.description":"Prints the active Serve configuration through the Tailscale.app executable.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeReset.title":"macOS app: Reset Serve","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.commands.macosDirectServeReset.description":"Clears the Serve configuration through the Tailscale.app executable if you need to start over.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copy":"Copy","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copied":"Copied","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copyCommandAria":"Copy {{command}} command","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.copyFailed":"Could not copy command: {{error}}","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.nextStep":"Copy the HTTPS MagicDNS URL from Serve status, append /mobile, paste it into the Phone Access URL field below, then create the QR code.","settings.components.settings.PhoneSetupGuideCard.funnelNote":"Use private tailnet Serve HTTPS for this setup. Public Funnel is not the recommended Phone Access path.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.eyebrow":"Docker node","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.title":"Start mobile-safe Docker node","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.description":"Install the Docker launcher once, then create a mobile-safe Docker node for recommended Android pairing.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.installStepTitle":"1. Install launcher once","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.directStepTitle":"2. Use direct commands","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.directStepDescription":"After install, these commands run locally and do not download the launcher again.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.workspaceModel":"The mobile-safe profile keeps private server state in Docker named volumes, binds published ports to localhost, avoids SYS_ADMIN/seccomp=unconfined, and does not create automatic shared host bind mounts.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.platform.macosLinux":"macOS / Linux","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.platform.windowsPowerShell":"Windows PowerShell","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.platform.installedCli":"Installed CLI","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.install.title":"Install autobyteus-docker","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.install.description":"Installs or replaces the local launcher and prints PATH or direct-path guidance.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.newContainer.title":"Create mobile-safe Docker node","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.newContainer.description":"Pulls the latest image and creates the next indexed mobile-safe container with an automatic local management credential.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.upgradeAll.title":"Upgrade all Docker nodes","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.upgradeAll.description":"Recreates all managed containers with the latest image while keeping named volumes.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.destroyAll.title":"Destroy all Docker nodes","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.destroyAll.description":"Removes all managed containers and unused old images while keeping named volumes.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.reset.title":"Reset Docker nodes","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.reset.description":"Destroys all managed containers, keeps volumes, then creates a fresh autobyteus-server-0.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspacePaths.title":"Show workspace paths","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspacePaths.description":"Prints the host folders backing /home/autobyteus/workspace and /home/autobyteus/shared.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspaceApplyAll.title":"Apply shared workspace to all nodes","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.workspaceApplyAll.description":"Safely recreates managed containers with the new bind mounts while keeping existing named volumes.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.storage.title":"Inspect Docker storage","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.storage.description":"Shows private named volumes, host bind mounts, and the launcher state directory.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.urls.title":"Show Docker node URLs","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.urls.description":"Prints the Backend URL again if you need to copy it later.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.status.title":"Show Docker node status","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.status.description":"Lists managed nodes and their current Docker status.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.logs.title":"Show Docker node logs","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.logs.description":"Prints recent logs for autobyteus-server-0 unless you pass another node name.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.stop.title":"Stop Docker node","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.commands.stop.description":"Stops autobyteus-server-0 by default without deleting named volumes.","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copy":"Copy","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copied":"Copied","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copyCommandAria":"Copy {{command}} command","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.copyFailed":"Could not copy command: {{error}}","settings.components.settings.DockerNodeStartGuideCard.nextStep":"After new-container prints Backend, paste that URL into Add Remote Node, open the Docker node window, then create the Phone Access QR there with a verified Android-facing HTTPS URL. Local mana